## 6. (Optional) Script: 20-cluster-info

If `kubectl` is present, show node status at a glance.
```bash
sudo tee /etc/update-motd.d/20-cluster-info > /dev/null <<'EOF'
#!/usr/bin/env bash

if command -v kubectl >/dev/null 2>&1; then
  READY=$(kubectl get nodes --no-headers 2>/dev/null \
    | awk '{s+=$2=="Ready"} END {print s "/" NR}')
  echo " Kubernetes Nodes Ready: ${READY}"
  echo
fi
EOF
sudo chmod +x /etc/update-motd.d/20-cluster-info
```

